Both read as inferences in the readiness handoff and in LANE.md. Measured from source, git, and the
filesystem, with no engine booted this session: gate 1 is NARROWER-THAN-CLAIMED and gate 5 FAILS.

Gate 1. The mechanism is REDIRECTION, not confinement: the wrappers move HOME so user:// resolves
elsewhere, and the process keeps full access to the player's directory throughout. Verified from
artifacts rather than from the comment claiming it -- a Godot user:// tree keyed to the canonical
checkout's ROOT hash sits under $TMPDIR, written by other lanes today. So does the counter-evidence:
four bare boots wrote into the player's REAL directory today, six days after the isolation landed.
The empirical witness does not travel with the run the gate is about, because only run_harness.sh
exports SF_PRODUCTION_SLOT and a journey run boots through with_machine.sh. It witnesses one file,
not the .bak the game itself falls back to; there is no sinkforge.save on this box, so its comparison
is absent-to-absent, which is the hazard the sentinel's own header identifies for the other slot; and
of the gate's three verbs, "cannot read" has no instrument at all. The lock is sound and has 26
properties behind it, but it is per-invocation and capped at 1800s, not per session.

Gate 5 names seven artifacts. The two tools cited as its evidence retain none of them: no video path
exists anywhere, capture_moments has a closed vocabulary of 40 poses and refuses any other name,
capture_manifest deliberately dropped its sha column and enumerates only tracked frames, and nothing
under tools/ writes a run receipt at all. EvalPlayerFeed's input log has no timestamp and no frame
index, so it is an order and not a cadence. The eighth item -- no canonical capture is overwritten --
is genuinely satisfied by four independent mechanisms, and it is one item out of eight.

Every claim is marked VERIFIED, SOURCE or UNVERIFIED, and the six runs that would settle the
remainder are written out with the output each must show. Two of them would show an instrument going
red; nothing else here rests on a guard anyone has watched fail.
