+## 1b. The redirect fails closed — SOURCE, and it is the one thing already fixed by a gate-1 audit
+
+`tools/with_machine.sh:57-59` refuses to boot when the isolated home cannot be created:
+
+    mkdir -p "$SF_HOME/.local/share" "$SF_HOME/.config" \
+        || { echo "!! could not create the isolated home at $SF_HOME — REFUSING to boot Godot against the" \
+            "player's real save slot. ..." >&2; exit 2; }
+
+`tools/run_harness.sh:175-176` does the same with `|| exit 2`. The comment at `with_machine.sh:47-56`
+records that this line used to be `if mkdir ...; then export HOME=...; fi` — failing **open**, into the
+player's real slot, silently — and that it was found by an earlier pass of this same gate (`e463767`,
+2026-08-17 23:08). So gate 1 has already caught one live defect of exactly the shape it is about.
+
+The refusal happens at line 57, before the argument check at line 82 and before the lock is taken at line
+96. A refused call therefore boots nothing and queues behind nobody.
+
+**UNVERIFIED — the exact run that settles it:**
+
+    SF_HOME=/dev/null/cannot-exist bash tools/with_machine.sh --headless --script res://tools/check_grid.gd
+    # must print "REFUSING to boot Godot against the player's real save slot", exit 2,
+    # and must NOT create the lock directory
+
+**What would make it fail:** the `||` branch being dropped, or the `export HOME` moving above the `mkdir`.
+Nothing in the harness watches for either — see 1e.
