+# Gate 5 — evidence feed
+
+> *"video or ordered captures, audio status, exact input cadence, commit, settings, seed, and save state
+> can all be retained without overwriting canonical captures."*
+
+Seven artifacts and one condition. The prior reading was *"likely satisfied — `tools/capture_moments.gd`
+and `tools/capture_manifest.sh` exist and retain captures without overwriting canonical ones."* That
+sentence is true and it is a receipt for the **condition**, which is the eighth item, not for any of the
+seven.
+
+## Item by item
+
+**1. Video or ordered captures — ABSENT.**
+
+    $ grep -rn -E 'write-movie|write_movie|movie_writer|MovieWriter|ffmpeg|\.avi' --exclude-dir=.git .
+    (no output)
+
+No video path of any kind. Godot's own `--write-movie` is used nowhere.
+
+Ordered captures do not exist either, and `capture_moments.gd` structurally cannot produce them. It is a
+**closed vocabulary of 40 named poses** — counted with `capture_manifest.sh`'s own extraction off the
+`match moment:` arms (`boot`, `delve`, `swing`, `counter`, …) — one PNG per process, each behind a full
+scene boot and a 60-frame settle. An unrecognised name is refused rather than saved (lines 429-434):
+
+    _:
+        printerr("capture_moments: unknown moment '%s' — refusing to save a boot frame under its name" % moment)
+        return 2
+
+So a journey runner cannot ask it for `_moment_0001.png`. Producing an ordered sequence means new code —
+a per-frame `get_root().get_texture().get_image().save_png(...)` loop — which does not exist. **Not a
+defect in `capture_moments.gd`: it is a posing instrument for the Sees tier and it is good at that. It is
+simply not the thing this gate names.**
+
+**2. Audio status — NOT RETAINED.** The state is reachable (`Settings.muted`, `AudioServer.is_bus_mute(0)`,
+exercised by `check_settings.gd:79-93`) and `EvalPlayerFeed.audio_enabled()` carries a flag for the actor's
+side. Neither capture tool records it. Note that `capture_moments._deafen` (line 155) is **input** deafness
+— `Controls.deaf`, `set_process_input(false)` — and has nothing to do with audio; reading it as an audio
+record would be the wrong instrument.
+
+**3. Exact input cadence — NARROWER THAN THE BRIEF STATES.** `EvalPlayerFeed._log` (`player_feed.gd:33`)
+appends one dictionary per input:
+
+    {"kind": "act",   "action": action, "pressed": pressed}
+    {"kind": "point", "px": px}
+    {"kind": "click", "button": button, "pressed": pressed}
+
+**There is no timestamp, no frame index, and no tick in any of them.** The log is an ORDER, and cadence is
+a rate; an order with no clock cannot express one. The protocol asks for cadence in two places — gate 5,
+and the scenario record's `feed: resolution, frame cadence, audio state` — and neither is answerable from
+this. Nothing persists the log to disk either; `input_log()` returns a copy to whoever holds the feed.
+Adding `Time.get_ticks_msec()` and `Engine.get_process_frames()` to each entry is a two-line change and
+would make this item true. Until then it covers input **order**, for the actor's side only.
+
+**4. Commit — RETAINED FOR SWEEPS, NOT FOR A JOURNEY RUN.** `run_harness.sh:1136` writes a header line with
+`tree`, `branch`, `head` and a `git diff HEAD | git hash-object` digest of the uncommitted delta. That is a
+real commit record and it is exactly the right shape. It is printed by the **harness runner**, which a
+journey run does not use.
+
+`capture_manifest.sh` does not supply it: lines 39-48 record that the sha column was **deliberately
+removed** ("an identifier that changes every time history is tidied"), leaving an author date and a
+renderer signature. It also enumerates by `git ls-files 'docs/media/moments/_moment_*.png'` (line 176), so
+its population is 52 tracked, committed frames. A journey run's captures would be untracked and outside
+that directory: the manifest would describe none of them, and `--check` would not notice they exist.
+
+**5. Settings — NOT RETAINED.** No tool snapshots `user://settings.cfg` or the resolution/zoom/feel state
+into a run record. `capture_moments` prints `zoom=%.2f` inside its `CAPTURED` line; that is one field of
+one frame, to stdout.
+
+**6. Seed — NOT RETAINED.** `capture_moments.gd` never prints a seed. The nearest thing in the repository
+is `play_tests.gd:56` (`"(game clock: %.0fx, world seed %d)"`), a different tool, printing to stdout. The
+protocol requires the seed in the scenario record, the receipt, and the population rule.
+
+**7. Save state — NOT RETAINED.** `save_sentinel.gd` computes exactly the digests this item wants and
+writes them to `$DIR/save_sentinel.state`, which lives in the harness log directory and is consumed and
+discarded by `verify`; the log directory itself is deleted when a run is clean. And per 1f the sentinel is
+not invoked outside `run_harness.sh` at all.
+
+**8. …without overwriting canonical captures — SATISFIED.** This is the one item with real engineering
+behind it, and four independent mechanisms hold it:
+
+- `SF_MOMENT_DIR` redirects the destination and nothing else, and **fails closed** — an unusable directory
+  refuses the capture rather than falling back to the repo root (lines 461-472);
+- an existing capture is copied to `_moment_prev/` before any write, and the capture is **refused** if the
+  copy fails, "because a capture is worth less than the capture it would destroy" (lines 509-521);
+  `_moment_prev/` is gitignored (`.gitignore:111`), so the undo generation is local;
+- a contamination gate runs **before** the shutter, so a wrong-scene frame never replaces a good one
+  (lines 479-486);
+- an unknown moment name is refused (lines 429-434).
+
+`capture_manifest.sh --check` is a registered layer (`run_harness.sh:338`) and asserts its own population
+before comparing (lines 196-210), so it cannot pass by describing nothing.
+
+## Gate 5 verdict: **FAILS**
+
+Seven artifacts named; **zero are retained by the two tools cited as the gate's evidence**. One (commit) is
+retained by a third tool for a different kind of run. One (input cadence) has an order-only log with no
+clock and no persistence. The condition — no canonical capture is overwritten — is genuinely satisfied and
+is one item out of eight.
+
+It fails because the retention pipeline **does not exist yet**, not because anything is broken. Nothing in
+`tools/` writes a run receipt at all:
+
+    $ grep -rln -E 'JSON\.stringify|store_string.*json|\.json"' tools/
+    (no output)
+
+The protocol's own receipt schema (`### Journey receipts`) lists commit, scenario ID, seed, actor profile,
+model/version, prompt hash, settings, controls, frame/audio feed, machine-lock status, timestamps, raw
+artifacts **and their checksums**. That is a superset of gate 5, and there is no writer for any of it. Gate
+5 is the smaller of the two jobs and it is unstarted.
+
+The cheapest honest close, in the same spirit as gate 6's: one receipt writer, run by the journey
+orchestrator, emitting a single file per session with those seven fields, plus timestamps on
+`EvalPlayerFeed._log`, plus an in-session frame writer under `SF_MOMENT_DIR`-style redirection so it
+inherits the non-overwriting property already proved. Then gate 5 becomes checkable by a layer that asserts
+the receipt has all seven keys and that none of them is empty — which is the form that cannot pass by
+describing nothing.
+
