Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:46:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] eval(gate5): stamp the input feed with two clocks, and
 cost the other six items

An order is not a cadence. _log recorded what came after what, and both the
gate and the scenario record ask for a rate, which a list with no clock in
it cannot express. _push now stamps frame and ms onto every entry before it
lands, in one helper rather than at four call sites, so a fifth input
cannot be added unstamped.

Two clocks because they answer different questions. frame is the tick the
game acted on, which a replay lines up against and which survives a scaled
clock. ms is wall time, which is what a rate needs and the only one of the
two that can show a stall: a hitch is a gap in wall time and is invisible
to a counter that only advances when a frame happens.

That closes item 3 of seven. The other six are BLOCKED rather than open,
and the receipt now says why and what they would cost: five of them are one
run-record artifact, and ordered captures are the only genuinely separate
piece of work. All six are harness expansion under a frozen A+ programme,
for an evaluation separately blocked at gate 6, so closing them would
unblock nothing.

Worktree-local. Disposable lane, no push from here.
